{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":18,"code":"JOB","name":"Job","testament":"OT"},"chapter":27,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"JOB 27:1"},"Moreover Job continued his parable, and said, ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"JOB 27:2"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["As"]}," God liveth, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["who"]}," hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["who"]}," hath vexed my soul; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"JOB 27:3"},"All the while my breath ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in me, and the spirit of God ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," in my nostrils; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"JOB 27:4"},"My lips shall not speak wickedness, nor my tongue utter deceit. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"JOB 27:5"},"God forbid that I should justify you: till I die I will not remove mine integrity from me. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"JOB 27:6"},"My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["me"]}," so long as I live. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"JOB 27:7"},"Let mine enemy be as the wicked, and he that riseth up against me as the unrighteous. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"JOB 27:8"},"For what ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the hope of the hypocrite, though he hath gained, when God taketh away his soul? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"JOB 27:9"},"Will God hear his cry when trouble cometh upon him? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"JOB 27:10"},"Will he delight himself in the Almighty? will he always call upon God? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"JOB 27:11"},"I will teach you by the hand of God: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," which ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is "]},"with the Almighty will I not conceal. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"JOB 27:12"},"Behold, all ye yourselves have seen ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it;"]}," why then are ye thus altogether vain? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"JOB 27:13"},"This ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," the portion of a wicked man with God, and the heritage of oppressors, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["which"]}," they shall receive of the Almighty. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"JOB 27:14"},"If his children be multiplied, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it is"]}," for the sword: and his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"JOB 27:15"},"Those that remain of him shall be buried in death: and his widows shall not weep. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"JOB 27:16"},"Though he heap up silver as the dust, and prepare raiment as the clay; ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"JOB 27:17"},"He may prepare ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it,"]}," but the just shall put ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["it"]}," on, and the innocent shall divide the silver. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"JOB 27:18"},"He buildeth his house as a moth, and as a booth ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["that"]}," the keeper maketh. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"JOB 27:19"},"The rich man shall lie down, but he shall not be gathered: he openeth his eyes, and he ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," not. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"JOB 27:20"},"Terrors take hold on him as waters, a tempest stealeth him away in the night. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"JOB 27:21"},"The east wind carrieth him away, and he departeth: and as a storm hurleth him out of his place. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"JOB 27:22"},"For ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["God"]}," shall cast upon him, and not spare: he would fain flee out of his hand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:22"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"23","sid":"JOB 27:23"},{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["Men"]}," shall clap their hands at him, and shall hiss him out of his place. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"JOB 27:23"}]}]}
